// @emit-error emitProgram: ref valtype with no interned shape
// FALSE-REJECT xfail — and the pin that keeps a COMPILER CRASH from coming back.
//
// A declared struct produced by a CALL, passed into a union parameter. The program is sound;
// the compiler refuses it. That reject is the gap. What this case exists to pin is the
// behaviour on the way to it: `emitUnionBoxArg` compared `sHeapIdx[bssi]` without the bounds
// check every other `sHeapIdx` reader carries, so a row that never interned a shape read PAST
// the array and the COMPILER TRAPPED — no diagnostic, just a wasm backtrace (#1611).
//
// #1611 filed it as a same-shape-union crash. The bisect says otherwise: neither the same
// shapes nor the `is` test is needed. `f(x: A | i32)` called as `f(mkA())` is enough, and the
// same value bound to a const first gets the loud reject instead. A CALL RESULT IN A UNION
// ARGUMENT POSITION is the trigger.
//
// EXPECTED eventually: compiles and prints 0. ACTUAL: the reject pinned above — but a
// diagnostic, which is what this case guards.
type A = { tag: i32, v: i32 }
function f(x: A | i32) { return 0 }
function mkA(): A { return { tag: 1, v: 9 } }
print(f(mkA()))
